        "id": "AI-AGGREGATION-29-001",
        "title": "Exact aggregation of 29 independent matrix products with a uniform cost gain",
        "origin": "Owner-directed Codex local combinatorial construction; external aggregation mechanism credited",
        "status": "proof-written-unreviewed",
        "evidence": "research/ai/2026-10-23-aggregation-families/proof.md",
        "statement": "For every positive integer n over every characteristic-zero field, an explicit family of 29 balanced tripartitions proves rank(M(n^3,n^3,n^3)^direct_sum29)<=x^9+9x^8+36x^7+3x^6, x=n+1. Complete set-based enumeration checks all 24389 mixed triples, of which 23072 off-diagonal terms vanish by centering and 1288 by 48 explicit corrections. The bound per output is strictly smaller than the cited external 28-product bound for every n, by the polynomial identity29*r28-28*r29=x^6*(x^3+9*x^2+7*x+32)>0.",
        "dependencies": [
          "Solomonik and Blaeser arXiv:2610.26563v2 centering and inclusion-exclusion aggregation; external ex28 comparison witness",
          "Exported29-product family and full exact mixed-triple certificate",
          "Written rational dual-embedding tensor identity over characteristic zero",
          "Weighted AM-GM and exact integer certificate for the displayed cost limitation"
        ],
        "limitations": "Weighted AM-GM with exact integer margin proves the stated rank upper-bound polynomial cannot reach 9/4 by direct asymptotic-sum substitution for any local dimension; this is not a lower bound on optimal tensor rank. Improves one attained finite aggregation family and its cost per output. No polynomial-source restriction, historical priority, independent mathematical review or Lean formalization is claimed. The scalar finite-field evaluation is an implementation control, not the uniform proof.",
        "independent_review": false,
        "lean_formalized": false,
