        "id": "AI-A4-TWOSIDED-RANKLOSS-001",
        "title": "Nine-direction rank-loss requirement for a full-source two-sided A4 conjugation",
        "section": "1-4",
        "statement": "Over C, conjugate the complete 112-dimensional normalized A4 slice space by I+t^-1 N, with the specified square-zero rank-sixteen source slice N=H_(0,0,0). Its complete saturated limit L acts by scalars on the stated twelve-dimensional subspace. For arbitrary constant full-rank maps P:C^112->C^110 and C:C^110->C^112, and an arbitrary Laurent first map, a degeneration to M(10,10,11) requires dim(P L C)<=103. Re-saturation recovers at most the number of lost leading directions, while the target has nonzero evaluation rank at least ten.",
